WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.289
On the Train.

2
00:00:01.569 --> 00:00:05.942
Day 25 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:08.716
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.996 --> 00:00:11.833
Railway stations are busy, loud and quick.

5
00:00:12.113 --> 00:00:15.804
Ask early, confirm twice, and keep your ticket and ID ready.

6
00:00:16.084 --> 00:00:18.324
These phrases work in India and abroad.

7
00:00:19.674 --> 00:00:20.527
Part 1.

8
00:00:20.807 --> 00:00:22.898
At the ticket counter or enquiry.

9
00:00:24.148 --> 00:00:25.129
You can ask:

10
00:00:25.409 --> 00:00:27.137
One ticket to Pune, please.

11
00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:29.679
Second AC or sleeper or general?

12
00:00:29.959 --> 00:00:30.791
(India).

13
00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:33.268
A return ticket to Manchester, please.

14
00:00:33.548 --> 00:00:34.892
Off-peak if possible.

15
00:00:35.172 --> 00:00:36.025
(UK).

16
00:00:36.305 --> 00:00:38.375
What time is the next train to Chennai?

17
00:00:38.655 --> 00:00:41.151
Is it a direct train, or do I need to change?

18
00:00:41.431 --> 00:00:43.073
Which platform does it leave from?

19
00:00:43.353 --> 00:00:44.996
How long does the journey take?

20
00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:49.759
Is there a cheaper option or railcard or senior discount?

21
00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:52.343
Can I cancel or change this ticket later?

22
00:00:52.623 --> 00:00:53.669
Is there a fee?

23
00:00:55.019 --> 00:00:55.893
Part 2.

24
00:00:56.173 --> 00:00:57.219
At the station.

25
00:00:58.469 --> 00:00:59.834
Here is a quick table:

26
00:01:00.114 --> 00:01:01.202
Ask, and When.

27
00:01:01.482 --> 00:01:05.237
Excuse me, is this the right platform for the Shatabdi to Mysore?:

28
00:01:05.517 --> 00:01:06.519
Before boarding.

29
00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.335
Has the platform changed?:

30
00:01:08.615 --> 00:01:10.962
When boards or announcements are confusing.

31
00:01:11.242 --> 00:01:12.757
Is the train running late?:

32
00:01:13.037 --> 00:01:14.039
Check delays.

33
00:01:14.319 --> 00:01:16.730
Where does coach B3 stop on the platform?:

34
00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.375
Long trains (India).

35
00:01:18.655 --> 00:01:21.087
Where's the waiting room or cloakroom or lift?:

36
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.391
Facilities.

37
00:01:22.671 --> 00:01:24.485
Does this train stop at Kalyan?:

38
00:01:24.765 --> 00:01:25.895
Confirm stops.

39
00:01:27.245 --> 00:01:28.141
Part 3.

40
00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.360
On the train.

41
00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.506
Your seat.

42
00:01:31.786 --> 00:01:33.962
Excuse me, I think this is my seat:

43
00:01:34.242 --> 00:01:35.927
32, coach S4.

44
00:01:36.207 --> 00:01:37.658
(show ticket politely).

45
00:01:37.938 --> 00:01:39.538
Would you mind swapping seats?

46
00:01:39.818 --> 00:01:41.546
I'd like to sit with my family.

47
00:01:41.826 --> 00:01:43.085
Is this seat taken?

48
00:01:43.365 --> 00:01:44.687
(unreserved trains).

49
00:01:44.967 --> 00:01:47.101
Could you help me lift my bag onto the rack?

50
00:01:48.451 --> 00:01:49.517
Co-passengers.

51
00:01:49.797 --> 00:01:52.272
Do you mind if I open or close the window?

52
00:01:52.552 --> 00:01:55.112
Could you please lower your voice or use headphones?

53
00:01:55.392 --> 00:01:56.629
I'm trying to sleep.

54
00:01:56.909 --> 00:01:59.213
Could you keep an eye on my bag for two minutes?

55
00:01:59.493 --> 00:02:00.901
Which station is next?

56
00:02:02.251 --> 00:02:04.833
Ticket examiner (TTE or conductor).

57
00:02:05.113 --> 00:02:06.478
Here is a quick table:

58
00:02:06.758 --> 00:02:08.529
They ask or say, and You say.

59
00:02:08.809 --> 00:02:09.897
Ticket, please.:

60
00:02:10.177 --> 00:02:11.137
Here you go.

61
00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:12.761
(ticket + ID).

62
00:02:13.041 --> 00:02:15.558
Your ticket is waitlisted or RAC.:

63
00:02:15.838 --> 00:02:17.587
Is there any berth available now?

64
00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:19.297
Could you allot one, please?

65
00:02:19.577 --> 00:02:20.857
You're in the wrong coach.:

66
00:02:21.137 --> 00:02:23.078
Sorry, which coach should I go to?

67
00:02:23.358 --> 00:02:25.406
This ticket isn't valid on this train.:

68
00:02:25.686 --> 00:02:27.478
I'm sorry, I didn't realise.

69
00:02:27.758 --> 00:02:28.995
What are my options?

70
00:02:29.275 --> 00:02:30.641
Can I pay the difference?

71
00:02:31.991 --> 00:02:32.908
Part 4.

72
00:02:33.188 --> 00:02:34.361
When things go wrong.

73
00:02:35.611 --> 00:02:36.635
Missed the train.

74
00:02:36.915 --> 00:02:37.854
You could say:

75
00:02:38.134 --> 00:02:41.441
Hi, I just missed the 6:15 train to Bangalore.

76
00:02:41.721 --> 00:02:45.369
Can I use this ticket on the next one, or do I need a new ticket?

77
00:02:45.649 --> 00:02:47.249
Can I get a partial refund?

78
00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:50.455
Train cancelled or very late.

79
00:02:50.735 --> 00:02:51.673
You could say:

80
00:02:51.953 --> 00:02:53.852
The 9 am train is cancelled.

81
00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:56.201
Is there an alternative train or bus?

82
00:02:56.481 --> 00:02:57.953
How do I claim a refund?

83
00:02:59.303 --> 00:03:00.327
Lost item.

84
00:03:00.607 --> 00:03:01.546
You could say:

85
00:03:01.826 --> 00:03:08.653
I left my laptop bag on the train that arrived at platform 4 at 10:30, coach A1, seat 22.

86
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:10.234
It's a black backpack.

87
00:03:10.514 --> 00:03:14.162
Where is the lost-property office, or who can I report it to?

88
00:03:15.512 --> 00:03:16.472
Part 5.

89
00:03:16.752 --> 00:03:17.819
Vocabulary.

90
00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:20.434
Here is a quick table:

91
00:03:20.714 --> 00:03:21.845
Word, and Meaning.

92
00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:23.063
Platform:

93
00:03:23.343 --> 00:03:24.581
Where the train stops.

94
00:03:24.861 --> 00:03:27.229
Berth (upper or middle or lower or side):

95
00:03:27.509 --> 00:03:29.087
Sleeping place (India).

96
00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.927
Waitlisted (WL) / RAC:

97
00:03:32.207 --> 00:03:34.597
Not yet confirmed or shared seat (India).

98
00:03:34.877 --> 00:03:35.687
Tatkal:

99
00:03:35.967 --> 00:03:37.994
Last-minute booking quota (India).

100
00:03:38.274 --> 00:03:39.554
Single or Return:

101
00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.818
One-way or round trip (UK).

102
00:03:42.098 --> 00:03:43.293
Peak or Off-peak:

103
00:03:43.573 --> 00:03:46.431
Busy (expensive) / quieter (cheaper) times.

104
00:03:46.711 --> 00:03:47.650
Change at...:

105
00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:49.743
Get off and take another train at...

106
00:03:50.023 --> 00:03:50.877
Terminus:

107
00:03:51.157 --> 00:03:52.607
Last station of the line.

108
00:03:53.957 --> 00:03:54.661
Fare:

109
00:03:54.941 --> 00:03:55.987
Ticket price.

110
00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.275
Part 6.

111
00:03:58.555 --> 00:03:59.985
Practice conversations.

112
00:04:01.235 --> 00:04:02.813
At the reservation counter.

113
00:04:03.093 --> 00:04:05.120
Here is how the conversation goes.

114
00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.488
Good morning.

115
00:04:06.768 --> 00:04:10.629
I'd like a ticket to Chennai on the Shatabdi tomorrow, please.

116
00:04:10.909 --> 00:04:11.827
Which class?

117
00:04:12.107 --> 00:04:13.941
Chair car or executive?

118
00:04:14.221 --> 00:04:15.331
Chair car.

119
00:04:15.611 --> 00:04:17.467
Is a window seat available?

120
00:04:17.747 --> 00:04:18.856
Let me check...

121
00:04:19.136 --> 00:04:21.952
Yes, seat 42 in C3 is a window seat.

122
00:04:22.232 --> 00:04:22.979
Great.

123
00:04:23.259 --> 00:04:24.603
How much is it?

124
00:04:25.953 --> 00:04:27.553
The conversation continues.

125
00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:33.721
1,145. rupeesPlease fill in this form with your name, age and ID number.

126
00:04:34.001 --> 00:04:35.067
Here you go.

127
00:04:35.347 --> 00:04:37.033
Can I pay by card?

128
00:04:37.313 --> 00:04:38.166
Yes.

129
00:04:38.446 --> 00:04:39.726
Here's your ticket.

130
00:04:40.006 --> 00:04:42.609
The train leaves at 6 am from platform 1.

131
00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:43.827
Thank you.

132
00:04:44.107 --> 00:04:45.750
Is there food included?

133
00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.843
Yes, breakfast is included.

134
00:04:49.193 --> 00:04:51.817
With the TTE about a waitlisted ticket.

135
00:04:52.097 --> 00:04:54.124
Here is how the conversation goes.

136
00:04:54.404 --> 00:04:55.684
Ticket, please.

137
00:04:55.964 --> 00:04:57.052
Here it is.

138
00:04:57.332 --> 00:04:59.913
It's still waitlisted, WL 3.

139
00:05:00.193 --> 00:05:02.327
Is there any berth available now?

140
00:05:02.607 --> 00:05:04.100
Let me check the chart...

141
00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:07.751
There's one side lower berth in S5 from Nagpur onwards.

142
00:05:08.031 --> 00:05:09.289
That would be great.

143
00:05:09.569 --> 00:05:11.703
Until Nagpur, can I sit here?

144
00:05:11.983 --> 00:05:13.412
Yes, you can sit here.

145
00:05:13.692 --> 00:05:16.508
I'll allot S5, berth 47, from Nagpur.

146
00:05:17.858 --> 00:05:19.458
The conversation continues.

147
00:05:19.738 --> 00:05:20.890
Thank you, sir.

148
00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.410
Do I need to pay anything extra?

149
00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.290
No, it's the same class.

150
00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:26.935
Thank you so much.

151
00:05:28.285 --> 00:05:29.821
That's the end of this lesson.

152
00:05:30.101 --> 00:05:34.773
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

153
00:05:35.053 --> 00:05:41.155
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

